total += dist[route[-1]][route[??]]
print(total)
```
answer: 0
wrong[1]: `route[1]` is place 2, so the last leg would go from 1 to 2 again (6) instead of back home (2): 21.
wrong[-1]: `route[-1]` is the last place, 1, so the leg would go from 1 to 1: 0 extra, 15 in all.
hint: The trip ends where it started.
hint: The starting place is the first item of `route`.
right: 0 → 2 is 9, 2 → 1 is 6, and back from 1 to 0 is 2: 17. Every brute-force route is measured like this, once for each of the (n − 1)! routes.
wrong: `route[0]`: the last leg goes from the last place, `route[-1]`, back to the first, `route[0]`.

